{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 8 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 8 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        int n = Integer.parseInt(br.readLine());\n        if (n > 20) {\n            System.out.println(0);\n            return;\n        }\n        int[][] pts = new int[n][5];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            String[] line = br.readLine().split(\"\\\\s+\");\n            for (int j = 0; j < 5; j++) {\n                pts[i][j] = Integer.parseInt(line[j]);\n            }\n        }\n        List<Integer> result = new ArrayList<>();\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            boolean isGood = true;\n            for (int j = 0; j < n && isGood; j++) {\n                if (i == j) continue;\n                for (int k = j + 1; k < n && isGood; k++) {\n                    if (k == i) continue;\n                    if (angleAt(pts[i], pts[j], pts[k]) < 90.0) {\n                        isGood = false;\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n            if (isGood) result.add(i + 1);\n        }\n        System.out.println(result.size());\n        for (int idx : result) {\n            System.out.println(idx);\n        }\n    }\n\n    static double angleAt(int[] o, int[] a, int[] b) {\n        double dot = 0, la = 0, lb = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i < o.length; i++) {\n            int vx = a[i] - o[i];\n            int vy = b[i] - o[i];\n            dot += vx * vy;\n            la += vx * vx;\n            lb += vy * vy;\n        }\n        return Math.toDegrees(Math.acos(dot / Math.sqrt(la * lb)));\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <cmath>\n#include <sstream>\n#include <string>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\ndouble angleAt(const vector<int>& o, const vector<int>& a, const vector<int>& b) {\n    double dot = 0, la = 0, lb = 0;\n    for (size_t i = 0; i < o.size(); i++) {\n        int vx = a[i] - o[i];\n        int vy = b[i] - o[i];\n        dot += vx * vy;\n        la += vx * vx;\n        lb += vy * vy;\n    }\n    return acos(dot / sqrt(la * lb)) * 180.0 / M_PI;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(0);\n    \n    string line;\n    getline(cin, line);\n    int n = stoi(line);\n    \n    if (n > 20) {\n        cout << 0 << endl;\n        return 0;\n    }\n    \n    vector<vector<int>> pts(n, vector<int>(5));\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        getline(cin, line);\n        istringstream iss(line);\n        for (int j = 0; j < 5; j++) {\n            iss >> pts[i][j];\n        }\n    }\n    \n    vector<int> result;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        bool isGood = true;\n        for (int j = 0; j < n && isGood; j++) {\n            if (i == j) continue;\n            for (int k = j + 1; k < n && isGood; k++) {\n                if (k == i) continue;\n                if (angleAt(pts[i], pts[j], pts[k]) < 90.0) {\n                    isGood = false;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        if (isGood) {\n            result.push_back(i + 1);\n        }\n    }\n    \n    cout << result.size() << endl;\n    for (int idx : result) {\n        cout << idx << endl;\n    }\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00016675988445058465, -3.3378546504536644e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.0001728385395836085, -1.311301275563892e-06, -5.125986263010418e-06, -1.311301275563892e-06, -7.867782187531702e-06, -2.50339189733495e-06, -0.0023411503061652184, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -1.0371154530730564e-05, -9.536738616588991e-07, -0.05617634207010269, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -5.1616290875244886e-05, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.19243201613426208, -0.0015041239093989134, -0.004079710692167282, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.07298051565885544, -0.16022592782974243, -0.14447686076164246, -1.7762025890988298e-05, -2.0265558760002023e-06, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -0.006848552729934454, -4.172316494077677e-06, -4.136476854910143e-05, -0.001378896413370967, -8.34461570775602e-06, -1.1444026313256472e-05, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -3.194758028257638e-05, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.3841830625315197e-06, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -2.7418097943154862e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -9.536738616588991e-07, -3.2186455882765586e-06, -2.9802276912960224e-06, -5.006777428206988e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -4.410734163684538e-06, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -9.250213042832911e-05, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -0.20142415165901184, -1.7404405298293568e-05, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -3.6954811548639555e-06, -4.768370445162873e-07, 0.0, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -2.7418097943154862e-06, -3.4450891689630225e-05, -0.002484213560819626, 0.0, -0.31327924132347107, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, 0.0